Subject: disable Incognito mode by default

Patches 0032, 0034, 0055, 0056, 0057 and 0069 close Incognito one entry point
at a time: the command, the app menu, the bookmark menus, the bookmark manager
and the --incognito switch. Upstream keeps adding doors - 153 introduced the
Isolated window and 154 put it into three more menus - and every door we have
not seen yet stays open. The side panel bookmarks menu is one of them: it asks
BookmarksSidePanelUI::IsIncognitoModeAvailable(), which reads the
IncognitoModeAvailability pref directly, and "Open in Incognito window" goes on
to BookmarkContextMenuController with an OFF_THE_RECORD disposition.

Upstream already has one switch for all of these, the IncognitoModeAvailability
policy. Make kDisabled its default in GOOROOM_BUILD so every reader of the pref
- IncognitoModePrefs::GetAvailability(), IsIncognitoAllowed(), CanOpenBrowser(),
ShouldLaunchIncognito() and the direct pref reads - sees Incognito as disabled
without a policy being deployed. The per-door patches stay; this is the net
under them.

Index: gooroom-browser-debian.git/chrome/browser/prefs/incognito_mode_prefs.cc
===================================================================
--- gooroom-browser-debian.git.orig/chrome/browser/prefs/incognito_mode_prefs.cc
+++ gooroom-browser-debian.git/chrome/browser/prefs/incognito_mode_prefs.cc
@@ -31,7 +31,11 @@
 
 // static
 const IncognitoModeAvailability IncognitoModePrefs::kDefaultAvailability =
+#if defined(GOOROOM_BUILD)
+    policy::IncognitoModeAvailability::kDisabled;
+#else
     policy::IncognitoModeAvailability::kEnabled;
+#endif
 
 // static
 bool IncognitoModePrefs::IntToAvailability(
